 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Constant cohomology of the affine line",
 "statement": "For $k$ finite or algebraically closed,\n\n$$\nH^q(\\mathbf A^1_{\\bar k},\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell)=\\begin{cases}\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell,&q=0,\\\\0,&q>0.\\end{cases}\n$$",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-fourier-transform/sk-lem-as-properties/lem-fd-affine-line-constant-cohomology.md",
  "place": "node lem-fd-affine-line-constant-cohomology, order 2684"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-fd-additive-character"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "The affine line is irreducible, hence connected, so $H^0=\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell$. For $q>0$ the $\\overline{\\mathbf Q}_\\ell$-cohomology is computed from the compatible finite-level cohomologies of the constant sheaves $\\mathbf Z/\\ell^n$ by [def-weil-pbc-qbar-category], and $H^q(\\mathbf A^1_{\\bar k},\\mathbf Z/\\ell^n)=0$ for every $q>0$: the vanishing for $q>1$ is the cohomological dimension of an affine curve of [sbc-thm-cohomological-dimension-of-an-affine-curve], and $H^1(\\mathbf A^1_{\\bar k},\\mathbf Z/\\ell^n)\\cong\\operatorname{Pic}(\\mathbf A^1_{\\bar k})[\\ell^n]=0$ by [thm-sc-affine-cohomology], the Picard group being trivial by [lem-sc-pic-affine] (the compactification is $\\mathbf P^1$ of genus $0$, whose Jacobian is trivial, so the quotient of [lem-sc-pic-affine] is $\\operatorname{Pic}(\\mathbf A^1)=0$).",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category",
    "sbc-thm-cohomological-dimension-of-an-affine-curve",
    "thm-sc-affine-cohomology",
    "lem-sc-pic-affine"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
